Toolchain compatibility only. devkitA64 r29's newlib declares timespec_get() without providing
it, so Mesa's static fallback in include/c11/threads.h clashed with the declaration; the fallback
keeps its body under its own name (mesa_timespec_get). No behaviour change: with the devkitPro
patches and this one, the libraries have the same symbols as the switch-mesa 20.1.0-5 package.

diff --git a/include/c11/threads.h b/include/c11/threads.h
index b512521..e66793e 100644
--- a/include/c11/threads.h
+++ b/include/c11/threads.h
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@
 #ifndef HAVE_TIMESPEC_GET
 #include <sys/time.h>
 
+/* Newer newlib (devkitA64 r29) declares timespec_get without providing it: keep Mesa's
+ * fallback under its own name so the two declarations do not clash. */
+#define timespec_get mesa_timespec_get
 static inline int
 timespec_get(struct timespec *ts, int base)
 {
